WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.060
We have interesting new polls from the last
two days.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.890
They are both terrible for Donald Trump.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.100
But I actually want to do a little bit more
of a deep dove and look at the internals of

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.130
one of these polls.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.630
So big picture, two new polls Tuesday poll
from Harvard.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.570
Harris says Biden is up 12.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:24.540
A poll from The New York Times today says
Joe Biden is up 14, which is absolutely stunning.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.789
But let's focus in on some of the details
of today's New York Times poll.

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:31.619
In this poll, Joe Biden is up fifty to 36.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:34.230
That's a 14 point lead.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.640
You also have 14 percent of respondents under
the other category.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.449
That includes people planning to vote, third
party people that are as yet undecided.

00:00:43.449 --> 00:00:46.460
So you still have a lot in that other category.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.210
Now, there are two particular areas that are
really hurting Donald Trump.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.370
Number one is his response to Corona virus.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:57.219
And number two is Trump's handling of race
relations.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:02.379
Sixty percent of the country believes Trump
has mishandled Corona virus.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.360
That's important because it is dramatically
higher than Trump's approval.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.570
And it shows us that there is a big net deficit
that Trump is experiencing thanks to his absolutely

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.100
disastrous handling of the virus.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.290
That includes among white voters and men.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:25.640
Typically, white voters and men favor Trump,
even among white voters and men.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.020
There is significant dissatisfaction with
Trump's handling of Corona virus then on race

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.020
relations.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.770
Sixty one percent of voters say they disapprove
of Trump's handling of race.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.850
Only 33 percent approve.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.890
These are two of the most one sided areas
where Trump is underwater.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:48.020
Now, a couple of other interesting things
from this poll.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.400
Democrats and Republicans right now, according
to The New York Times poll, equally support

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.600
their party's candidates.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.050
It is independents that are sort of making
the difference for Joe Biden.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.659
So take a look at this.

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:03.600
Eighty five percent of Democrats say they're
going to vote for Joe Biden.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.060
Eighty five percent of Republicans say they're
going to vote for Donald Trump.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.080
That's even.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.069
There are actually more Republicans nationally
than Democrats.

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:13.799
So in a sense, that favors Donald Trump.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:21.120
But independents are leaning towards Biden
by a twenty one point margin, which is huge.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:27.799
And then also interesting, the Trump campaign
has been pushing the idea that Biden is too

00:02:27.799 --> 00:02:29.480
old to be president.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.819
Remember, Trump turns 74 about 10 days ago.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.329
Joe Biden, 77.

00:02:34.329 --> 00:02:40.760
As of right now, 60 percent of voters disagree
that Joe Biden is too old.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.719
So we don't know what's going to happen between
now and November.

00:02:44.719 --> 00:02:50.440
But the key numbers I'm looking at are, number
one, an incumbent president polling only 36

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.959
percent four months before the election is
not good, number two.

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.510
And let me say a little bit more about that
in head to head reelection campaign.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:05.299
So when you've had a strong third party candidate,
the numbers are different when you really

00:03:05.299 --> 00:03:08.340
have a head to head matchup for president.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:14.470
The the worst performing incumbent president
was John Adams, who got 39 percent of the

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.749
vote in eighteen hundred.

00:03:16.749 --> 00:03:23.390
Even the wildly unpopular Herbert Hoover still
got 40 percent of the vote against FDR in

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.810
1932.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:28.810
I don't think Trump will be under 40 no matter
what.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:35.019
But if Trump ends up with anywhere close to
where he's polling now, 40 to 44, even 45

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:38.109
percent of the vote, this could be a historic
defeat.

00:03:38.109 --> 00:03:39.109
If.

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:40.299
We actually go out and vote.

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:42.629
That's no, that's one metric that's important.

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:46.530
Trump polling in the 30s, four months before
the election.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:52.049
The other really important metric is that
Joe Biden is regularly polling over 50 percent,

00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:54.440
50 percent or more in polls.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:59.829
If you look at polling at this point in 2016,
Hillary Clinton was only occasionally polling

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:00.829
50 percent.

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:04.590
And when she was, it really didn't go any
higher than 51, 52.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:09.459
Joe Biden is regularly polling 50 percent
or even more.

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:13.920
And the reason that matters is that the undecided
vote.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.069
The unsure vote.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:20.200
The third party vote, as you get closer to
Election Day, it often will consolidate or

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.790
move towards the incumbent.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.440
In this case, the incumbent is Trump.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.100
What matters about Biden regularly being at
50 percent or more is that Biden doesn't need

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:35.140
to get any more support to win if we don't
get complacent and go out and vote.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.020
We could see the economy tick up a little
bit if Corona virus gets under control.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.380
It's only a blowout in November.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.100
If we go out and vote, and that's a real question
mark.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:50.750
So now that we've looked at all the polls,
what you should do is go out there pretending

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.570
as if every single one of these polls says
Trump is winning by one.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:55.570
Right.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.830
The idea the mentality you should have is
I don't care what the polls are.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:05.050
I need to act as if my vote alone could give
a state to Joe Biden.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:09.680
Of course, it's not literally the case, but
that's the attitude that we should have.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.810
And we'll continue following the polls.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:16.540
We'll continue following Trump's internals
among independents on corona virus, on race

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.610
relations.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:22.480
But in the end, at the end of the day, we
all need to say on November 3rd, what would

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:27.100
I be doing right now if my vote could be the
vote that swings this election from Trump

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.100
to Biden?

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.450
Oh, I'd go out and vote.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.730
That's exactly what I'm going to do.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.910
And of course, many of us will vote early.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:34.800
Many of us will be voting absentee.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.320
And that just means we have the opportunity
to lock our vote in even sooner.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:07:25.030
We don't even have

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:28.030
to wait until November.

